## 2. Target Users

### 2.1 Primary Persona (v1 focus)
**"Casual Chris"** — everyday gym-goer
- Goes to the gym 2–4x/week, no formal program
- Currently tracks via Notes app, memory, or not at all
- Wants to see progress and stay consistent, not chase elite performance
- Logs in-gym on phone; reviews progress later on laptop

### 2.2 Future Personas (unlocked in later phases)
| Persona | Description | Core Need | Phase |
|---|---|---|---|
| The Beginner | New to fitness, intimidated by gyms | Guided onboarding, starter programs | Phase 1 |
| The Optimizer | Experienced lifter tracking PRs | Deep analytics, customization | Phase 1–2 |
| The Time-Crunched Parent | 20–30 min/day, home workouts | Efficiency, flexible programming | Phase 2 |
| The Hybrid Athlete | Mixes strength, running, mobility | Unified cross-discipline programming | Phase 3 |

### 2.3 Core User Needs (v1)
1. Log sets/reps/weight quickly while resting between sets
2. See what they lifted last time for a given exercise
3. See simple progress trends (are they getting stronger?)
4. Stay motivated through streaks, PRs, visible progress
5. Not feel overwhelmed by features they don't need yet

