## 3. Scope by Phase

This is the key structural change from the two source docs: FitAll's full feature set becomes a **roadmap**, not a v1 spec.

| Phase | Focus | Key Features |
|---|---|---|
| **Phase 1 (v1 Launch)** | Nail workout tracking | Logging, history/PRs, templates, progress dashboard, offline mobile, web review |
| **Phase 2** | Expand the daily habit | Nutrition logging (barcode scan), recovery/sleep sync, wearable connections, adaptive programming |
| **Phase 3** | Broaden the discipline | GPS cardio/run tracking, mobility/meditation library, unified cross-discipline dashboard |
| **Phase 4** | Retention & growth loops | Social (friends, opt-in leaderboards, challenges), badges/achievements, referral loops |

Phase gates are retention-based, not calendar-based: **do not begin Phase 2 build until Phase 1 hits 35%+ four-week retention.** This directly addresses FitAll's own identified risk.

