## 4. Phase 1 Features (Launch Scope, Detailed)

### 4.1 Onboarding
- Goal selection (build muscle, get stronger, general consistency)
- Experience level self-assessment
- Optional starter template selection (e.g., "Push/Pull/Legs," "Full Body 3x/week")
- Guest mode to try the app before account creation (local-only, prompts to save)

**Acceptance criteria:** User reaches home dashboard in ≤5 steps and ≤3 minutes.

### 4.2 Workout Logging
- Start a workout in ≤2 taps ("Start Empty Workout" or "Repeat Last Workout")
- Add exercises from a searchable library (200+ exercises, categorized by muscle group/equipment)
- Log sets: weight, reps, optional RPE and notes
- Auto-fills previous weight/reps as a starting suggestion
- Built-in rest timer, offline-capable
- Mark complete; auto-saves duration

**Acceptance criteria:** Logging screen responds in ≤1s; full offline support with sync on reconnect.

### 4.3 Exercise History & PRs
- Per-exercise history (date, sets, weight, reps)
- PR detection and highlighting ("New PR! 🎉")
- Simple graph: weight/volume over time per exercise

### 4.4 Workout Templates
- Save any completed workout as a reusable template
- Pre-built starter templates for new users
- Reorder/edit exercises within a template

### 4.5 Progress Dashboard
- Weekly/monthly workout count and streak tracker
- Total volume lifted over time
- Optional manual body-weight log
- Calendar view of workout days

### 4.6 Platform & Sync
- **Mobile (iOS/Android):** primary in-gym use, offline-first, optimized for one-handed/sweaty-hands use, <2s cold start
- **Web:** full feature parity for history, templates, and library browsing; not optimized for live logging but functional
- Real-time account-based cloud sync between mobile and web

