## 7. Future Phases (Detailed)

### Phase 2: Nutrition, Recovery, Wearables
- Food logging: search, barcode scan, AI photo-assisted estimate (target: <2s match for 90% of common packaged foods)
- Macro/calorie targets tied to goal
- Sleep tracking via wearable sync or manual entry
- Readiness score (sleep + HRV if available + recent training load)
- Wearable connections: Apple Watch, Garmin, Whoop, Fitbit
- Adaptive programming: adjusts difficulty based on logged performance and missed sessions

### Phase 3: Cardio & Broader Discipline
- GPS-based run/ride/walk tracking (pace, distance, elevation, splits)
- Interval and race-training plans
- Guided mobility/stretching routines
- Short meditation/breathing library
- Unified analytics dashboard spanning strength + cardio + recovery

### Phase 4: Social & Growth Loops
- Friend connections, activity feed
- Opt-in group challenges (step count, workout streaks)
- Privacy-respecting, opt-in leaderboards
- Badges/achievements
- Smart reminders based on user's typical workout time; streak-protection nudges

