## 10. Risks & Open Questions

### Risks
- **Feature bloat undermining onboarding simplicity** — mitigated structurally by the phase-gate model above (not just "progressive disclosure UX")
- **Scope creep pressure** post-launch to accelerate Phase 2 before retention data justifies it — needs explicit stakeholder buy-in on the retention gate now
- Wearable API dependencies (rate limits, deprecations) could break sync reliability once Phase 2 begins
- Food-photo AI accuracy may frustrate users if too low — needs fallback to manual entry
- Architecting Phase 1 data models to support Phase 2–4 without a rebuild adds upfront engineering cost — needs early buy-in from eng leadership

### Open Questions
- Do we support bodyweight/cardio exercises differently from strength (reps/weight vs. time/distance) even in Phase 1, to ease the Phase 3 transition?
- What's the exercise library source — licensed database or built in-house? (Also relevant to Phase 3 video demo content — do we build or license?)
- Should Phase 1 remain fully free, or introduce a lightweight premium tier (e.g., unlimited templates) ahead of Phase 2 to start monetization learning earlier?
- What's the wearable integration priority order for Phase 2 — Apple Watch vs. Garmin vs. Whoop?
- Should social features (Phase 4) be opt-in by default or on from day one?

