## 11. Appendix

### 11.1 Competitive Landscape
Strava (cardio-first), Strong/Hevy (strength-first), MyFitnessPal (nutrition-first), and Whoop (recovery-first) each own one slice of the fitness journey. This product's differentiation is sequencing: win strength-tracking first with the focus of a Strong/Hevy competitor, then expand into the others' territory only once the core habit is proven — arriving at FitAll's original breadth-plus-personalization vision without the onboarding cost of trying to be everything at launch.

### 11.2 Assumptions
- Users primarily lift weights (strength training) rather than pure cardio, based on the "gym-goer" persona
- Users already have gym access; the app doesn't handle membership or facility access
- Single-user accounts for Phase 1 (family sharing arrives with Premium+ in Phase 2)
